{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for startup-time-to-release (issue #468, part of #412). Same per-(process, supply) instantiation as sim/closed-loop-startup/testbench/closed_loop_startup.request.json.tmpl (issue #414); the DUT is the schematic (design/netlist/bandgap_{core,amp,startup}.spice, carried verbatim in the body).",
    "The 45-point grid (5 processes x 3 temperatures x 3 supplies) runs as 15 requests of 3 temperatures each: the runner image's single-models.lib channel carries one process per request (klayout-tools#2668), and the PWL ramp is this bench's convergence path so the supply axis cannot ride `corners.supply_v` (`alter` would clobber it). The temperature axis rides `corners.temperature_c` natively.",
    "THE CHECKPOINT LADDER LIVES HERE. This is the one thing that makes this bench not a duplicate of closed-loop-startup: `measurements[]` below samples the five release-criteria signals (det, i_mkfb, fb, sns1, sns2) at eleven fixed times -- 100 200 300 400 500 600 700 800 900 1000 2000 us -- instead of one final checkpoint, plus the two t=20us `*_early` points the legacy template also carries. 11 x 5 + 2 = 57 entries, one per `meas tran` line of testbench/tb_startup_time_to_release.spice.tmpl, which stays in place as the point-definition reference.",
    "Single source of truth for the ladder (issue #210): the legacy bench derived it from its template's own `.meas` block rather than hardcoding it, and that property is preserved -- sim/harness/enrich_supply_bench_report.py --bench startup_release reads the ladder back off the `det_<N>u_v` measurement names in the report this request produces, so adding or removing a checkpoint here is the only edit needed and the two can never drift.",
    "Measurement naming: ngspice `.meas` names in the legacy template are `v_det_<N>u` / `i_mkfb_<N>u`; this repo's klt records name the same quantity `det_<N>u_v` / `i_mkfb_<N>u_a` (the legacy CSV's own column spelling, and the convention sim/closed-loop-startup's request already follows). The record spec's `pass_requires` and run_klt_sim.sh's sanity anchors use these same names.",
    "Every column is a single-vector `.meas ... at=<t>` over a resident `.save` vector. The derived dvsns_<N>u_v columns, the per-checkpoint verdicts and release_time_us are applied by sim/harness/enrich_supply_bench_report.py, the same practice the committed records use. Values arrive at 6 significant figures.",
    "The supply is held from 200 us to 2 ms (the same window the legacy bench and sim/closed-loop-startup use), so the 2000u checkpoint is directly comparable with closed-loop-startup's own t=2ms record.",
    "`remote.hosts: 3` = one fleet job per temperature point (the box-TC wrapper's measured split, scaled to this grid; not separately measured here)."
  ],
